  "goodToKnow": "Der Stundenlohn is an hourly wage: ein Stundenlohn von 15 Euro brutto. Germany introduced a statutory Mindestlohn (minimum wage) in 2015 at 8.50 euros; an independent commission sets increases, and it is 13.90 euros in 2026. Der Lohn is a wage, often hourly or for manual work, while das Gehalt is a monthly salary. Brutto means before tax, netto after. Plural: die Stundenlöhne."
